  "question": {
    "text": "For an exothermic reaction, following two steps are involved.<br />\r<br />\r<math> <mrow> <mtable> <mtr> <mtd> <mtext mathvariant=\"bold\">Step 1.</mtext> </mtd> <mtd> <mtext>A</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>B</mtext> <mo>→</mo> <mtext>I</mtext> </mtd> <mtd> </mtd> <mtd> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>slow</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mtd> </mtr> <mtr> <mtd> <mtext mathvariant=\"bold\">Step 2.</mtext> </mtd> <mtd> <mtext>I</mtext> <mo>&nbsp;→</mo> <mtext>AB</mtext> </mtd> <mtd> </mtd> <mtd> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>fast</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mtd> </mtr> </mtable> </mrow> </math><br />\r<br />\rWhich of the following graphs correctly represent this reaction ?",
